      RAVEN4  TRAIN + GENERATE          9
      BIGRAM MARKOV TEXT GENERATOR USING1
      DESCRIPTION LISTS.                1
      TEXT  FIRST 12 LINES OF THE RAVEN,1
      115 TOKENS, 83 DISTINCT WORDS (SEE1
      RAVEN4.VOCAB).                    1
      EVERY WORD IS A REGIONAL SYMBOL   1
      T1..T83, AND IS ALSO A DESCRIBABLE1
      LIST (A HEAD CELL, INITIALLY      1
      EMPTY).                           1
      A WORD S DESCRIPTION LIST HOLDS   1
      ITS SUCCESSORS  EACH ATTRIBUTE IS 1
      A WORD THAT FOLLOWED IT IN THE    1
      TEXT, AND ITS VALUE IS AN INTEGER 1
      DATA TERM COUNTING HOW OFTEN. ONLY1
      SUCCESSORS ACTUALLY SEEN ARE      1
      STORED, SO THE TABLE IS SPARSE.   1
      TEXT FOR OUTPUT  AN ALPHANUMERIC  1
      DATA TERM HOLDS ONLY 5 CHARACTERS,1
      SO EACH WORD IS SPELLED BY A LIST 1
      YN OF PIECES V..  A FLAG CHARACTER1
      PLUS UP TO 4 LETTERS, + FOR THE   1
      FIRST PIECE OF A WORD AND - FOR A 1
      CONTINUATION (POND ERED = +POND   1
      -ERED). THE MAP TN -  YN IS THE   1
      DESCRIPTION LIST OF ONE SEPARATE  1
      DESCRIBABLE LIST X4. IT IS KEPT   1
      OUT OF THE SUCCESSOR LISTS BECAUSE1
      J16 TRAPS ON NON-NUMERIC VALUES.  1
      G4 PRINTS ONE WORD BY PRINTING ITS1
      PIECES  THE DECODER JOINS THEM.   1
      PHASE 0 (LABEL)  ATTACH THE TEXT  1
      TERMS. PHASE 1 (TRAIN)  FOR EACH  1
      ADJACENT PAIR (PREV, THIS) OF THE 1
      TEXT LIST X1, ADD 1 TO THE COUNT  1
      OF THIS IN PREV S DESCRIPTION     1
      LIST, CREATING IT WITH COUNT 1 IF 1
      IT IS NEW (ROUTINE G2).           1
      PHASE 2 (GENERATE)  REPEAT N      1
      TIMES  J16 PICKS A SUCCESSOR OF   1
      THE CURRENT WORD AT RANDOM,       1
      WEIGHTED BY THE COUNTS (ROUTINE   1
      G1).                              1
      WORKING CELLS (W0-W2 ARE AVOIDED  1
      J11 AND OTHER LIBRARY ROUTINES    1
      OVERWRITE THEM)  W9 CURRENT WORD, 1
      W4 PREVIOUS WORD, W6 CURRENT TEXT 1
      CELL, W5 THIS WORD, W7 FIRST WORD,1
      W8 STEP COUNTER.                  1
      DEFINE REGIONS                    2 A0            2
      LIST REGION                       2 L0            900
      TOKEN REGION                      2 T0            85
      SUPPORT LIST REGION               2 X0            6
      ROUTINE REGION                    2 G0            6
      NUMBER REGION                     2 N0            4
      TEXT-PIECE REGION                 2 V0            133
      PIECE-LIST REGION                 2 Y0            85
      ATTRIBUTE KEY REGION              2 K0            3
      SIZES  T0/V0 = VOCABULARY + 2. X0 1
      HOLDS THE THREE SUPPORT LISTS X1  1
      (TEXT), X2 (WORDS), X3 (TEXT      1
      TERMS). X4 IS THE WORD -  TEXT    1
      MAP, K2 A TABLE SEPARATOR MARK.   1
      REGION L0 SUPPLIES CELLS FOR THE  1
      PUSHDOWN STACK AND FOR THE        1
      DESCRIPTION LISTS AND COUNTS BUILT1
      DURING TRAINING.                  1
      ROUTINE HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=0.       5       00
      --- MAIN PROGRAM A0 ---           1
      PHASE 0  BUILD THE TEXT MAP. LIST 1
      X2 HOLDS THE WORD SYMBOLS T1..T83 1
      AND LIST X3 THE MATCHING PIECE    1
      LISTS Y1..Y83 IN THE SAME ORDER.  1
      WALK BOTH IN STEP AND DO J11 ON   1
      LIST X4  ASSIGN (1) AS VALUE OF   1
      ATTRIBUTE (0) OF LIST (2), I.E.   1
      PUSH X4, THEN THE TEXT TERM, THEN 1
      THE ATTRIBUTE.                    1
      PUSH WORD LIST X2                   A0    10X2
      J60  (0) = FIRST WORD CELL                  J60
      W3 = WORD CELL  POP                       20W3
                                                10X3
      (0) = FIRST PIECE-LIST CELL                 J60
      W6 = PIECE-LIST CELL  POP                 20W6
      MAP LOOP  PUSH MAP LIST X4 = (2)    9-4   10X4
                                                11W6
      (0) = PIECE LIST (VALUE (1))                J80
                                                11W3
      (0) = WORD SYMBOL (ATTRIBUTE (0))           J80
      J11  X4 WORD  = PIECE LIST                  J11
                                                11W3
      NEXT WORD CELL                              J60
      IF H5-, ALL LABELLED  GO 9-5              709-5
      W3 = NEXT WORD CELL                       20W3
                                                11W6
                                                  J60
      NEXT TEXT CELL  LOOP                      20W6    9-4
      POP LEFTOVER CELL                   9-5     J8
      PHASE 1  TRAIN. START AT THE HEAD 1
      CELL OF THE TEXT LIST AND STEP TO 1
      ITS FIRST CELL WITH J60 (LOCATE   1
      NEXT CELL).                       1
      PUSH TEXT LIST HEAD X1                    10X1
      J60  (0) = FIRST TEXT CELL                  J60
      W6 = FIRST CELL  POP                      20W6
      READ THE WORD IN THAT CELL WITH   1
      J80 (SYMBOL IN CELL)  IT IS THE   1
      PREVIOUS WORD W4. KEEP A COPY IN  1
      W7 SO THE LAST WORD CAN WRAP      1
      AROUND TO THE FIRST.              1
      PUSH CONTENTS OF W6 (THE CELL)            11W6
      J80  (0) = WORD IN CELL                     J80
      W4 = PREVIOUS WORD  POP                   20W4
                                                11W4
      W7 = FIRST WORD                           20W7
      TRAINING LOOP, LABEL 9-1. STEP TO 1
      THE NEXT TEXT CELL. J60 SETS H5+  1
      IF THERE WAS ONE, H5- AT THE END  1
      OF THE LIST  70 9-9 BRANCHES TO   1
      9-9 WHEN H5-.                     1
      LOOP  PUSH CURRENT CELL             9-1   11W6
      J60  (0) = NEXT CELL, SET H5                J60
      IF H5-, TEXT ENDED  GO 9-9                709-9
      W6 = NEXT CELL  POP                       20W6
                                                11W6
      (0) = WORD IN THAT CELL                     J80
      W5 = THIS WORD  POP                       20W5
      G2  COUNT PAIR (W4 -  W5)                   G2
                                                11W5
      W4 = W5  GO BACK TO 9-1                   20W4    9-1
      9-9  TRAINING DONE. J60 LEFT THE  1
      LAST CELL ON THE STACK WHEN IT    1
      FAILED  J8 POPS IT. THEN CLOSE THE1
      CYCLE BY COUNTING THE PAIR (LAST  1
      WORD W4 -  FIRST WORD W7) SO NO   1
      WORD IS A DEAD END.               1
      POP LEFTOVER CELL                   9-9     J8
                                                11W7
      W5 = FIRST WORD                           20W5
      G2  COUNT PAIR (W4 -  W5)                   G2
      PRINT THE CONTINUATION TABLE  FOR 1
      EVERY WORD ON THE WORD LIST X2,   1
      PRINT A SEPARATOR CARD (K2), THEN 1
      CALL G3, WHICH PRINTS THE WORD    1
      AND, FOR EACH SUCCESSOR, ITS TEXT 1
      FOLLOWED BY ITS COUNT. A FINAL    1
      SEPARATOR ENDS THE TABLE.         1
                                                10X2
                                                  J60
      W3 = FIRST WORD CELL                      20W3
      TABLE LOOP  PUSH WORD CELL          9-6   11W3
      (0) = WORD SYMBOL                           J80
      W9 = WORD TO PRINT  POP                   20W9
                                                10K2
      PRINT SEPARATOR ****                        J152
      G3  PRINT WORD + ITS SUCCESSORS             G3
                                                11W3
      NEXT WORD CELL                              J60
      IF H5-, TABLE DONE  GO 9-7                709-7
      W3 = NEXT CELL  LOOP                      20W3    9-6
      POP LEFTOVER CELL                   9-7     J8
                                                10K2
      PRINT END-OF-TABLE MARK ****                J152
      PHASE 2  GENERATE. W9 = FIRST     1
      WORD  PRINT IT WITH J152 (PRINT   1
      SYMBOL).                          1
      PUSH FIRST WORD                           10T1
      W9 = CURRENT WORD  POP                    20W9
                                                10X4
                                                11W9
      J10  PIECE LIST OF WORD                     J10
      G4  PRINT ITS TEXT                          G4
      STEP COUNTER W8 IS A FRESH COPY   1
      (J120) OF THE CONSTANT ZERO N2, SO1
      J125 (ADD 1) DOES NOT CHANGE THE  1
      CONSTANT.                         1
                                                10N2
      J120  COPY OF ZERO                          J120
      W8 = COUNTER = 0                          20W8
      GENERATION LOOP, LABEL 9-2. J116  1
      TESTS (0)   (1)  PUSH THE LIMIT N11
      FIRST, THEN THE COUNTER. 70 9-3   1
      LEAVES THE LOOP WHEN THE TEST     1
      FAILS (H5-).                      1
      LOOP  PUSH LIMIT N1 (=(1))          9-2   10N1
      PUSH COUNTER (=(0))                       11W8
      J116  H5+ IF COUNTER   LIMIT                J116
      IF H5-, DONE  GO 9-3                      709-3
      G1  MAKE AND PRINT ONE WORD                 G1
                                                11W8
      J125  ADD 1 TO COUNTER, LEAVE (0)           J125
      J8 POPS (0)  GO BACK TO 9-2                 J8    9-2
      9-3  HALT                           9-3     J7    0
      ROUTINE HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=0.       5       00
      --- G1  ONE GENERATION STEP ---   1
      INPUT  W9 = CURRENT WORD. OUTPUT  1
      W9 = NEXT WORD, AND ITS TEXT (J10 1
      ON THE MAP X4 GIVES ITS PIECE     1
      LIST, THEN G4 PRINTS IT) IS       1
      PRINTED.                          1
      J16 TAKES A DESCRIBABLE LIST (THE 1
      CURRENT WORD) AND RETURNS ONE OF  1
      THE ATTRIBUTES OF ITS DESCRIPTION 1
      LIST (A SUCCESSOR WORD), CHOSEN AT1
      RANDOM WITH PROBABILITY           1
      PROPORTIONAL TO THE INTEGER COUNT 1
      VALUE.                            1
      PUSH CURRENT WORD                   G1    11W9
      J16  (0) = WEIGHTED RANDOM SUCCESS          J16
      W9 = NEXT WORD  POP                       20W9
                                                10X4
                                                11W9
      J10  PIECE LIST OF NEW WORD                 J10
      G4  PRINT TEXT  END OF G1                   G4    0
      ROUTINE HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=0.       5       00
      --- G3  PRINT ONE WORD AND ITS    1
      CONTINUATIONS ---                 1
      INPUT  W9 = WORD. OUTPUT (ONE CARD1
      EACH)  THE WORD S TEXT, THEN FOR  1
      EVERY SUCCESSOR ITS TEXT AND ITS  1
      COUNT.                            1
      THE WORD S DESCRIPTION LIST IS    1
      NAMED IN THE HEAD OF THE WORD S   1
      LIST, SO J80 ON THE WORD GIVES IT.1
      ITS CELLS ALTERNATE ATTRIBUTE (A  1
      SUCCESSOR WORD), VALUE (ITS       1
      COUNT), ATTRIBUTE, VALUE...       1
      CELLS  W4 CURRENT DESCRIPTION-LIST1
      CELL, W5 SUCCESSOR, W6 COUNT.     1
      PUSH MAP X4                         G3    10X4
                                                11W9
      J10  PIECE LIST OF THE WORD                 J10
      G4  PRINT WORD TEXT                         G4
                                                11W9
      J80  (0) = DESCRIPTION LIST NAME            J80
      J60  (0) = FIRST ATTRIBUTE CELL             J60
      W4 = ATTRIBUTE CELL  POP                  20W4
      LOOP 9-3  READ THE SUCCESSOR (W5),1
      STEP TO THE VALUE CELL AND READ   1
      THE COUNT (W6), THEN PRINT BOTH.  1
      LOOP  PUSH ATTRIBUTE CELL           9-3   11W4
      (0) = SUCCESSOR SYMBOL                      J80
      W5 = SUCCESSOR                            20W5
                                                11W4
      J60  VALUE CELL                             J60
                                                20W4
                                                11W4
      (0) = COUNT                                 J80
      W6 = COUNT                                20W6
                                                10X4
                                                11W5
      J10  PIECE LIST OF SUCCESSOR                J10
      G4  PRINT SUCCESSOR TEXT                    G4
                                                11W6
      PRINT ITS COUNT                             J152
      ADVANCE  PUSH CELL                        11W4
      J60  NEXT ATTRIBUTE CELL                    J60
      IF H5-, NO MORE  GO 9-7                   709-7
      W4 = NEXT CELL  LOOP                      20W4    9-3
      POP LEFTOVER CELL  END OF G3        9-7     J8    0
      ROUTINE HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=0.       5       00
      --- G4  PRINT ONE WORD S TEXT --- 1
      INPUT  (0) = THE WORD S PIECE LIST1
      YN. OUTPUT  ONE CARD PER PIECE    1
      (E.G. +POND THEN -ERED). J60 STEPS1
      THROUGH THE LIST CELLS  J80 GIVES 1
      THE PIECE (AN ALPHANUMERIC DATA   1
      TERM) IN A CELL  J152 PRINTS IT.  1
      CELL W7 HOLDS THE CURRENT LIST    1
      CELL.                             1
      J60  (0) = FIRST PIECE CELL         G4      J60
      W7 = PIECE CELL  POP                      20W7
      LOOP  PUSH PIECE CELL               9-1   11W7
      (0) = PIECE                                 J80
      PRINT IT                                    J152
                                                11W7
      NEXT PIECE CELL                             J60
      IF H5-, NO MORE  GO 9-2                   709-2
      W7 = NEXT CELL  LOOP                      20W7    9-1
      POP LEFTOVER CELL  END OF G4        9-2     J8    0
      ROUTINE HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=0.       5       00
      --- G2  COUNT ONE BIGRAM ---      1
      INPUT  W4 = PREVIOUS WORD, W5 =   1
      THIS WORD. EFFECT  THE COUNT OF W51
      IN W4 S DESCRIPTION LIST GOES UP  1
      BY 1  IT IS CREATED WITH COUNT 1  1
      IF W5 WAS NOT THERE.              1
      J10 = FIND VALUE OF ATTRIBUTE (0) 1
      OF LIST (1)  PUSH THE LIST W4     1
      FIRST, THEN THE ATTRIBUTE W5. IF  1
      FOUND (H5+) THE VALUE, AN INTEGER 1
      DATA TERM, IS LEFT AS (0)  IF NOT 1
      (H5-) NOTHING IS LEFT.            1
      PUSH LIST = PREVIOUS WORD           G2    11W4
      PUSH ATTRIBUTE = THIS WORD                11W5
      J10  FIND COUNT  SET H5                     J10
      IF H5- (NEW PAIR), GO 9-5                 709-5
      FOUND  J125 ADDS 1 TO THE COUNT IN1
      PLACE AND LEAVES IT AS (0)  J8    1
      POPS IT. THEN SKIP THE CREATE     1
      STEP.                             1
      J125  COUNT = COUNT + 1                     J125
      POP COUNT  GO 9-6                           J8    9-6
      9-5 NEW PAIR  J11 = ASSIGN (1) AS 1
      VALUE OF ATTRIBUTE (0) OF LIST    1
      (2). PUSH LIST W4, THEN A FRESH   1
      COPY OF THE CONSTANT ONE N3 (J120 1
      SO THE CONSTANT IS NOT SHARED),   1
      THEN THE ATTRIBUTE W5. J11 CREATES1
      THE DESCRIPTION LIST IF IT DOES   1
      NOT EXIST YET.                    1
      PUSH LIST (2)                       9-5   11W4
                                                10N3
      J120  NEW COUNT CELL = 1 (1)                J120
      PUSH ATTRIBUTE (0)                        11W5
      J11  ADD (W5 -  1) TO W4                    J11   0
      9-6  END OF G2 (NO-OP)              9-6     J0    0
      DATA HEADER. TYPE=5,Q=1.          5       01
